B.azD=new A.F("Anansi and the Box of Stories","In the beginning, all the world's stories belonged to Nyame, the sky god. Anansi the spider wanted them for the people, so Nyame set him a price: bring me Onini the python, Osebo the leopard and Mmoboro the hornets. Anansi tricked each one with his wit, climbed back up his web with all three, and Nyame gave him the golden box of stories. He opened it over the villages, and that is why we tell stories by the fire to this day. (An Akan folktale, retold.)")
B.azN=new A.F("The Tortoise and the Birds",'When famine came, the birds were invited to a feast in the sky. Tortoise begged each bird for a feather so he could fly with them, and went along. He tricked the birds by taking the name "All of You", so the feast food was for him. Angry, the birds took back their feathers, and Tortoise fell to the earth, which is why his shell is cracked. (A West African folktale, retold.)')
B.azr=new A.F("Why the Sun and Moon Live in the Sky","Long ago Sun and Moon lived on earth and visited their friend Water. Water built a bigger and bigger house, until his people filled it and the water rose up to the roof. Sun and Moon had to climb into the sky to stay dry, and they have lived there ever since. (A Nigerian folktale, retold.)")
